-- room for one more child: under sixteen answering at once, go on; at sixteen, wait for one to finish
-- (wait4 blocking on any child); a connection waiting meanwhile is held by the kernel's queue. A public
-- answer reads one kept file, so a child holds little beyond the pages it shares with the server; sixteen
-- keep a slow reader from holding up the rest
s-room : Word → Proc W Word
s-room n = if wlt n #16 then ret {lzero} {W} n else bind (sys-call #61 #18446744073709551615 #0 #0 #0 #0 #0) (λ r → ret {lzero} {W} (if wlt r #9223372036854775808 then wsub n #1 else #0))
